      "content": "That self-critical voice is a symptom of deep hurt, not proof of actual moral failure. The \"hollow\" feeling you describe is often a desperate attempt to give weight to a painful event by labeling yourself \"bad,\" when in reality, you are feeling the crushing emotional weight of a \"good\" heart that is still learning how to cope. Please consider speaking with a counselor to help you separate these painful self-accusations from the facts of the situation.",
      "source": "target",
